# Development is on Windows, CI runs on ubuntu-latest. Without this, line
# endings depend on whoever cloned the repo and on their core.autocrlf setting,
# which is the same class of cross-platform mismatch that running CI on Linux is
# meant to catch.
#
# Everything text is normalised to LF in the repository. Checkouts still get
# native endings where a tool needs them.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, never normalised. The walkthrough media in particular would be
# silently corrupted by newline translation.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.gif  binary
*.mp4  binary

# CIF fixtures are compared byte-for-byte against what COD served, and their
# checksums are how their provenance is verifiable at all.
*.cif  -text
